;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-14, for Phase 17 (design section 20,
;; proposal 9, approved by the user); reviewed by the user, 2026-10-14. It
;; replaces the file the user reviewed on 2026-10-13. Why this is right:
;; - Card and CardHex are new (proposal 9): Card makes the digits in a
;;   32-byte frame buffer with FORMATTEDTEXT_CARD and writes them with
;;   Field in width n (CVTWL 4(AP), the stream); CardHex makes them with
;;   FORMATTEDTEXT_CARDHEX and writes them with String. The two
;;   .EXTERNALs, FormattedText's key and the module's own (.IDENT,
;;   POC_K1_) are new. Every line number after them is 19 more, the
;;   trap's PUSHL included.
;; The rest is as the user reviewed it on 2026-10-13:
;; - FormattedOutput is rtl/llvm's procedures over LineOutput: each
;;   procedure's first parameter is the stream, an INTEGER (MOVW 4(AP)),
;;   passed on as a longword (CVTWL) to LINEOUTPUT_CHAR, _STRING, _LN,
;;   _INT and _HEX, which do the writing as before.
;; - String copies its value open array s on entry (MOVC3 in pieces of at
;;   most 65535 bytes, onto the stack), as any value open array is, then
;;   passes the copy's address and length to LINEOUTPUT_STRING.
;; - Int and Hex copy their two HUGEINTs (MOVQ @8(AP), @12(AP)) and pass
;;   each as the address of a quadword copy (MOVAQ), as any HUGEINT value
;;   parameter is.
;; - Ten passes e as a longword to FORMATTEDTEXT_TEN and returns its
;;   G_floating result in R0 and R1; a function that reached its END
;;   would trap (12).
;; - Field, local (no .ENTRY, not universal), is the Field that Out and
;;   Err each had, with n a HUGEINT: blanks := n minus the text's length
;;   (FORMATTEDTEXT_LENGTH, widened by ASHL #-31 and subtracted with
;;   SBWC), then one LINEOUTPUT_CHAR of 32 while blanks > 0 (the quadword
;;   compared high longword first), then LINEOUTPUT_STRING of the text.
;; - Real copies x (MOVF) and n, has FORMATTEDTEXT_REAL write the text
;;   into a 32-byte local (FormattedText.maxText), then calls Field with
;;   n widened to a quadword. LongReal is the same with the LONGREAL
;;   passed as the address of a copy (MOVG).
;; - Its initializer calls LINEOUTPUT_INIT, then FORMATTEDTEXT_INIT.
;; - On the guest every fixture that prints through Out or Err prints
;;   what it printed before, through this module.
; FormattedOutput, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
	.TITLE	FORMATTEDOUTPUT
